<resources>
    <!--
      The OAuth 2.0 *Web application* client ID from Google Cloud Console
      (APIs & Services -> Credentials). Not the Android one.

      Credential Manager is given this as its serverClientId, and it is what
      Google puts in the token's "aud" claim - which is what the server
      checks in kk_google_claims(). The Android client ID never appears in
      the token; it is what lets Play Services vouch for this app, and it is
      matched by package name and signing certificate instead.

      Left empty on purpose. GoogleSignInClient.isConfigured reads this, and
      the Google buttons stay hidden while it is blank, so a build without a
      Google project simply does not offer sign-in rather than offering it
      and failing. Same shape as kk_google_configured() on the server.

      Not a secret - a web client ID is public by design and ships in every
      client. It is safe in version control.
    -->
    <string name="google_web_client_id" translatable="false">167811151941-m9uta3oajtv9gpj6lmrk21gbtq60vq30.apps.googleusercontent.com</string>
</resources>
